 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c27c9fb7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# PINN — Tamil Nadu Groundwater Level\n",
    "\n",
    "Trains a physics-informed neural network for the 2D transient unconfined groundwater flow equation:\n",
    "\n",
    "`S(x,y) * dh/dt = div(T(x,y) * grad(h)) + R(x,y,t) - Q(x,y,t)`\n",
    "\n",
    "`S`, `T` are learned per-district scalars (inverse problem). Inputs are the Phase 1 outputs\n",
    "`observations.csv` and `collocation.csv`, read from the Kaggle dataset\n",
    "`benadictinfanta/water-data` (see the config cell for `DATA_DIR`) — see `DATA_DICTIONARY.md` and\n",
    "`STATUS.md` in the project repo for what each column means and every known data-quality caveat\n",
    "(sign convention, missingness, etc).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Run this on Kaggle with a GPU and internet access enabled** — it was authored on a CPU-only\n",
    "machine and not run there. `DATA_DIR`/`OUTPUT_DIR` are set to Kaggle paths permanently; for Colab,\n",
    "change them per the comment in the config cell.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "168b6600",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# --- GPU/torch compatibility guard (Run 21) ---------------------------------\n",
    "# Kaggle's bundled torch (2.10.0+cu128) dropped support for cc < 7.0 GPUs. The\n",
    "# free GPU pool sometimes hands out a Tesla P100 (sm_60, cc 6.0), which then\n",
    "# dies with \"CUDA error: no kernel image is available\" on the first matmul.\n",
    "# Detect the device's compute capability in a throwaway subprocess (so we don't\n",
    "# import torch into the main session prematurely) and, only if it is < 7.0,\n",
    "# install a torch build that still ships sm_60 kernels. T4/A100/L4 (cc >= 7.0)\n",
    "# are untouched and keep the current torch with an identical run.\n",
    "import subprocess, sys\n",
    "det = subprocess.run(\n",
    "    [sys.executable, \"-c\",\n",
    "     \"import torch as t; \"\n",
    "     \"print('CAP', t.cuda.get_device_capability(0) if t.cuda.is_available() else 'cpu')\"],\n",
    "    capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=120)\n",
    "print(\"torch probe:\", det.stdout.strip() or det.stderr.strip().splitlines()[-1])\n",
    "cap = None\n",
    "if det.returncode == 0:\n",
    "    for tok in (det.stdout or \"\").split():\n",
    "        if tok.startswith(\"CAP\"):\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            cap = tuple(int(x) for x in tok.strip(\"() \").split(\",\") if x.strip())\n",
    "            break\n",
    "        except ValueError:\n",
    "            pass\n",
    "if cap is None:\n",
    "    print(\"no usable GPU/capability -- leaving bundled torch in place\")\n",
    "elif cap[0] < 7:\n",
    "    print(f\"GPU cc {cap} needs sm_60 support: installing torch 2.5.1+cu118 \"\n",
    "          f\"(supports cc 5.0-9.0) BEFORE importing torch in this session\")\n",
    "    r = subprocess.run([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pip\", \"install\", \"-q\",\n",
    "                        \"torch==2.5.1\",\n",
    "                        \"--index-url\", \"https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu118\"],\n",
    "                       text=True, timeout=1800)\n",
    "    verify = subprocess.run([sys.executable, \"-c\",\n",
    "                             \"import torch; print('now', torch.__version__)\"],\n",
    "                            capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=300)\n",
    "    print(\"verify:\", (verify.stdout or verify.stderr).strip())\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f\"GPU cc {cap} >= 7: bundled torch stays (unchanged behavior for cc>=70 runs)\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7b47ccce",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import math\n",
    "import time\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import requests\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "import torch.nn as nn\n",
    "import torch.nn.functional as F\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "device = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\n",
    "print(f\"torch {torch.__version__}, device = {device}\")\n",
    "if device.type == \"cuda\":\n",
    "    print(f\"GPU: {torch.cuda.get_device_name(0)}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ed44dd6a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Config\n",
    "\n",
    "Single path variable + all hyperparameters/weights up top, nothing buried later."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3f5be66b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# --- paths --------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "# Kaggle paths, set permanently (dataset: benadictinfanta/water-data).\n",
    "# For Colab instead: DATA_DIR = \"/content/drive/MyDrive/pinn_predict/data/processed\"\n",
    "DATA_DIR = \"/kaggle/input/datasets/benadictinfanta/water-data\"\n",
    "OBSERVATIONS_PATH = os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"observations.csv\")\n",
    "COLLOCATION_PATH = os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"collocation.csv\")\n",
    "OUTPUT_DIR = \"/kaggle/working/\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- elevation (depth -> head conversion, see STATUS.md issue 2/4) --------\n",
    "# No DEM ships in data/raw/, so this is fetched at runtime from a free SRTM\n",
    "# API rather than added to the Phase 1 pipeline -- see the \"Elevation lookup\"\n",
    "# cell for why. Cached to ELEVATION_CACHE_PATH so re-runs (e.g. after\n",
    "# restarting the kernel) don't re-fetch ~4,000 points from scratch.\n",
    "ELEVATION_API_URL = \"https://api.opentopodata.org/v1/srtm30m\"\n",
    "ELEVATION_BATCH_SIZE = 100      # public server limit\n",
    "ELEVATION_RATE_LIMIT_S = 1.0    # public server limit: 1 request/second\n",
    "ELEVATION_MAX_RETRIES = 3\n",
    "ELEVATION_CACHE_PATH = os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, \"elevation_cache.csv\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- model architecture ---------------------------------------------------\n",
    "EMBEDDING_DIM = 8\n",
    "# Run 19: per-well baseline as an INPUT FEATURE instead of a learned embedding.\n",
    "# Run 18's per-well embedding (WELL_EMBEDDING_DIM) was REVERTED after it overfit: the net\n",
    "# memorized each well's identity on the train window and extrapolated to 383m beyond the\n",
    "# 100m H_MAX clip (see STATUS.md eighteenth-run entry).  The thing persistence (5.50m, the\n",
    "# forecast baseline) actually knows is each well's LAST OBSERVED DEPTH BEFORE THE CUTOFF --\n",
    "# so we hand the network that number directly (h0, normalized as h0hat) instead of making\n",
    "# it re-learn per-well baselines as free parameters.  The net then only has to model the\n",
    "# trend/seasonality ON TOP of the anchor, which is far easier than reconstructing baselines\n",
    "# from (x,y,elev).  Held-out wells and collocation points have NO anchor (0 in normalized\n",
    "# units = the global mean), so the spatial task is unchanged and stays honest.\n",
    "H0_DROPOUT_P = 0.3        # Run 20: fraction of TRAINING rows whose anchor is zeroed (both the\n",
    "                          # input slot AND the additive residual).  Run 19 leaned hard on the\n",
    "                          # anchor (first-layer weight 0.334 vs ~0.20 on every other input), so\n",
    "                          # held-out wells (h0hat=0) were out-of-distribution and the spatial\n",
    "                          # metric regressed to 13.45m.  Dropout makes the unanchored case a\n",
    "                          # regular part of training -- see the model cell for the residual form.\n",
    "HIDDEN_WIDTH = 64               # cut from 128 after the \"accuracy\" run (RMSE 12.49m, just barely\n",
    "                                 # losing to the 12.07m district-mean baseline): pred-vs-actual showed\n",
    "                                 # smooth looping bands instead of a noisy cloud around the diagonal --\n",
    "                                 # a sign the 101K-param net is riding a low-dimensional shortcut\n",
    "                                 # (embedding + a smooth function of t) rather than resolving real\n",
    "                                 # well-to-well variation, which (x,y) alone can't fully explain anyway\n",
    "                                 # (STATUS.md issue 4 -- h is depth, not head, so local ground elevation\n",
    "                                 # leaks into \"spatial\" variation no smooth field can capture). Smaller\n",
    "                                 # net + more weight decay, re-test RMSE against the same baseline.\n",
    "                                 # The fifth run (2026-07-19) showed this alone doesn't close the gap --\n",
    "                                 # see the elevation/head cells below, which address issue 4 directly.\n",
    "NUM_HIDDEN_LAYERS = 4            # cut from 7, same reasoning\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- training h range (a MODELING choice, logged loudly -- see STATUS.md) --\n",
    "# Phase 1's clean_groundwater.py drops |h| >= 200 as sentinels, which is too loose:\n",
    "# h is p50=6.1m, p99=54m, but the surviving range runs to +-199.97m. Those 0.08% of\n",
    "# rows contribute ~29 to the MSE on their own (~5.4m of RMSE) and are not physically\n",
    "# plausible depth-to-water for Tamil Nadu. Rows outside this range are EXCLUDED from\n",
    "# training and evaluation, and the count is printed. Widen/narrow and re-run to see\n",
    "# the sensitivity; this is not a claim that every excluded row is bad data.\n",
    "# NOTE: this filter is applied to raw depth `h`, before the elevation/head conversion\n",
    "# below -- the sentinel cut is about bad readings, not about head vs. depth.\n",
    "H_MIN = -5.0                   # small negative = artesian/near-surface, plausible (median\n",
    "                                # negative is only -1.9m); the -65m..-199m tail is not.\n",
    "H_MAX = 100.0\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- loss weights (kept explicit, not buried in the loss function) --------\n",
    "W_DATA = 1.0\n",
    "W_PDE = 1e-4                   # Run 12: BACK DOWN from Run 11's 3.7e-2, which caused a regression.\n",
    "                                # Run 11 raised it 373x alongside the head->depth target switch, to\n",
    "                                # \"hold the physics/data balance constant\". That reasoning was wrong.\n",
    "                                # It preserved the ratio of loss VALUES, but in Run 10 the PDE was\n",
    "                                # already ~98% of the total loss and merely INERT (its curve was flat\n",
    "                                # noise -- an ineffective gradient). Preserving that dominance was\n",
    "                                # only safe while it stayed inert. The target switch made the PDE\n",
    "                                # gradient effective (Run 11's pde loss actually fell, 1000 -> 70),\n",
    "                                # and the preserved dominance then overrode the data fit: data loss\n",
    "                                # dipped to ~0.32 by step ~1000, then ROSE to ~0.55 and plateaued.\n",
    "                                # At 1e-4 with the depth target the PDE contributes ~10% of the total\n",
    "                                # instead of ~82% -- sub-dominant, which is what it should have been.\n",
    "                                # See STATUS.md eleventh-run entry.\n",
    "                                # tuning history (held-out wells, same split every run):\n",
    "                                # Pre-head-conversion runs (depth target -- PDE was wrong quantity):\n",
    "                                #   1e-4 -> RMSE 15.6m, T frozen at softplus(0) for all 38 districts\n",
    "                                #   1e-2 -> RMSE 18.3m, T spread (0.52-1.65) for 26 districts with R\n",
    "                                #   1e-3 -> RMSE 18.1m, T mostly back at init -- worst of both\n",
    "                                #   ALL THREE lose to the district-mean baseline (RMSE 12.07m).\n",
    "                                # Post-head-conversion runs (head = elev-h target, PDE now correct):\n",
    "                                #   1e-6 -> RMSE 11.78m, MAE 6.77m -- first run to beat baseline\n",
    "                                #           convincingly; S/T frozen (W_PDE negligible), Run 7.\n",
    "                                #   1e-4 -> RMSE 11.86m, MAE 7.02m (Run 8, 2026-07-24): still beats\n",
    "                                #           baseline but T stayed BYTE-IDENTICAL to Run 7's frozen\n",
    "                                #           softplus(0) despite the 100x weight increase, and the pde\n",
    "                                #           loss curve was flat noise the whole run -- raising W_PDE\n",
    "                                #           did nothing because T's only gradient path (the Laplacian\n",
    "                                #           term) was apparently already near zero, not just weighted\n",
    "                                #           too low. See STATUS.md eighth-run entry.\n",
    "                                #   1e-4 -> Run 9 (2026-07-24): W_PDE held at Run 8's value; the\n",
    "                                #           change was LAPLACIAN_SCALE (see below) + Tanh->SiLU.\n",
    "                                #           T unfroze but RMSE regressed to 12.14m -- LAPLACIAN_SCALE\n",
    "                                #           too strong; Run 10 backs it off. See STATUS.md.\n",
    "                                # NOTE: data loss = MSE on NORMALIZED head (shrank by ~head_s^2 vs\n",
    "                                # the old depth-MSE). 1e-4 here is roughly equivalent in relative\n",
    "                                # weight to the old 1e-6 * head_s^2 rescale, but with the PDE now\n",
    "                                # governing the correct physical quantity so a meaningful gradient\n",
    "                                # can flow to S/T for the first time.\n",
    "W_IC = 1.0\n",
    "IC_WINDOW_DAYS = 60             # observations within this many days of the training set's earliest\n",
    "                                # timestamp are treated as \"initial condition\" points. There is no clean\n",
    "                                # gridded h(x,y,t=0) snapshot in the data (readings are sparse and\n",
    "                                # irregular in time), so this is a practical stand-in, not a true IC.\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- delta (residual-from-anchor) regularization (Run 21) ---------------------------------\n",
    "# The Run 20 residual form makes the model predict h0hat + mlp(...), i.e. it STARTS at\n",
    "# persistence and adds a learned deviation delta = mlp(...).  Locally re-scoring Run 20\n",
    "# showed the net deviates from the anchor on 539/699 forecast wells and WINS on only 160\n",
    "# (STATUS.md twentieth-run entry): the extrapolated train-window trend adds error instead\n",
    "# of removing it, leaving PINN at 6.54m vs persistence 5.50m.  W_DELTA penalizes mean(delta^2)\n",
    "# so the model only moves off the anchor when the data gives it a strong reason -- a soft\n",
    "# \"persistence is the floor\" prior that shrinks useless trend extrapolation toward zero.\n",
    "W_DELTA = 1e-2\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- PDE diffusion-term non-dimensionalization (added for Run 9, see STATUS.md) -----------\n",
    "# A local smoke test (real cached elevations, few epochs, CPU) instrumented with the new\n",
    "# |laplacian| diagnostic (see pde_residual/training-loop cells) showed the physical Laplacian\n",
    "# is ~1e-11 EVEN AT EPOCH 0 -- not something that develops or vanishes over training, a fixed\n",
    "# consequence of the chain-rule conversion head_s / x_s^2 (head varies ~200m; x spans Tamil\n",
    "# Nadu's ~700km width in METERS, so x_s ~ 91,000m and x_s^2 ~ 8e9). T only receives gradient\n",
    "# through `-T_d * laplacian`, so at this scale T's contribution to the residual is ~11 orders\n",
    "# of magnitude smaller than R/Q (O(1-20)) -- invisible to gradient descent regardless of\n",
    "# activation function or W_PDE, which is why Run 8's 100x W_PDE bump did nothing and why the\n",
    "# Tanh -> SiLU swap alone (Model cell) is not expected to fix this by itself.\n",
    "# LAPLACIAN_SCALE multiplies ONLY the diffusion term's contribution inside pde_residual (not\n",
    "# T_raw's parametrization -- get_T() is unchanged) to make that gradient path visible again.\n",
    "# Calibration history:\n",
    "#   3e11 -> Run 9 (2026-07-24): sized so T_d*SCALE*|laplacian| ~ O(1-10), comparable to R/Q.\n",
    "#           T unfroze (spread 0.44-2.73) BUT RMSE regressed to 12.14m (lost to the 12.07m\n",
    "#           baseline) and spatial_maps.png's range collapsed to -20..35m, losing the correct\n",
    "#           Western Ghats deep-water signal -- the diffusion term, being a function of the\n",
    "#           network's OWN curvature, was strong enough to reshape the MLP's spatial weights and\n",
    "#           overwrite the good Run 7/8 elevation fit. Too strong. See STATUS.md ninth-run entry.\n",
    "#   1e10 -> current (Run 10): 30x smaller, sizing the diffusion term to ~O(0.4) -- a SUB-DOMINANT\n",
    "#           regularizer (well under R/Q's O(1-20)) instead of a competing objective. A local\n",
    "#           smoke test confirms T still gets real gradient here (|T_raw.grad| ~1.7e-3 at 30\n",
    "#           epochs, ~11 orders of magnitude above the ~1e-14 frozen-T noise floor), just far\n",
    "#           more gently, so the network's data-driven fit should survive. If this STILL regresses\n",
    "#           vs Run 7 (11.78m), see STATUS.md: frozen-T Run 7 is the accuracy reference and\n",
    "#           learning T at all is a deliberate accuracy-vs-physics trade, not a value to keep tuning.\n",
    "# IMPORTANT CAVEAT: R and Q are documented proxies without true SI calibration (Q is a\n",
    "# unitless [0,1] index, not m3/day -- DATA_DICTIONARY.md limitation 4), so there was never a\n",
    "# path to recovering literal m2/day transmissivity from this residual as posed. LAPLACIAN_SCALE\n",
    "# does not fix that -- it only makes T learnable AT ALL (real cross-district variation) instead\n",
    "# of frozen. Treat learned_S_T_per_district.csv's T column as a RELATIVE quantity (compare\n",
    "# districts to each other) after this change, not literal transmissivity, unless R/Q are\n",
    "# recalibrated to true SI units in a future revision.\n",
    "LAPLACIAN_SCALE = 1e10\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- training ---------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "HELD_OUT_WELL_FRACTION = 0.15\n",
    "# --- Run 12: FORECAST split (see STATUS.md twelfth-run entry) --------------------------\n",
    "# Runs 7-11 were scored only on held-out WELLS. Local diagnostics showed that task is at its\n",
    "# feature ceiling: kNN(x,y) on train well means scores 11.62m vs the PINN's best 11.51m, because\n",
    "# 73.6% of h's variance is BETWEEN-well and is not spatially smooth -- no smooth f(x,y,elev) can\n",
    "# interpolate it at an unmonitored location. Splitting on TIME instead gives real headroom\n",
    "# (trivial baselines 5.55-5.71m, oracle floor 3.73m) and matches the actual use case: predicting\n",
    "# groundwater at monitored wells going forward. Both tasks are now reported; forecast is primary.\n",
    "TEMPORAL_CUTOFF_QUANTILE = 0.80   # train on t below this quantile of observation time, evaluate\n",
    "                                  # at/above it. 0.80 -> t~20057d (~2024.9), a ~1.2-year horizon\n",
    "                                  # over ~810 wells / ~906k rows.\n",
    "BATCH_SIZE_DATA = 4096\n",
    "BATCH_SIZE_COLLOC = 4096\n",
    "BATCH_SIZE_IC = 512\n",
    "N_EPOCHS_ADAM = 20000\n",
    "ADAM_LR = 1e-3\n",
    "WEIGHT_DECAY = 3e-4             # bumped from 1e-4 alongside the smaller network above -- same\n",
    "                                # memorization concern ((x,y) uniquely identifies a well, so the net\n",
    "                                # can just memorize the ~2,655 training wells: train RMSE ~5m vs\n",
    "                                # held-out 15.6m on the very first run).\n",
    "LR_STEP_SIZE = 5000\n",
    "LR_GAMMA = 0.5\n",
    "PRINT_EVERY = 500\n",
    "RUN_LBFGS_FINETUNE = False   # Run 22: Run 21's L-BFGS stepped Adam's data loss back up\n",
    "                              # (0.26 ~ 5.3m depth -> 0.52 ~ 7.4m). The fine-tune fights\n",
    "                              # the weighted objective; keep the better Adam fit.\n",
    "LBFGS_MAX_ITER = 500\n",
    "\n",
    "SEED = 0\n",
    "torch.manual_seed(SEED)\n",
    "np.random.seed(SEED)\n",
    "os.makedirs(OUTPUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9d0aafa9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Load data\n",
    "\n",
    "Raises immediately if either file is missing or malformed -- never falls back to synthetic\n",
    "placeholder data (see CLAUDE.md)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "336150ee",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "REQUIRED_OBS_COLS = {\"x\", \"y\", \"t\", \"district\", \"h\", \"R\", \"Q\"}\n",
    "REQUIRED_COLLOC_COLS = {\"x\", \"y\", \"t\", \"district\", \"R\", \"Q\"}\n",
    "\n",
    "if not os.path.exists(OBSERVATIONS_PATH):\n",
    "    raise FileNotFoundError(\n",
    "        f\"{OBSERVATIONS_PATH} not found. This notebook requires the Phase 1 output; \"\n",
    "        f\"set DATA_DIR to wherever it's mounted. Refusing to generate synthetic data instead.\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "if not os.path.exists(COLLOCATION_PATH):\n",
    "    raise FileNotFoundError(\n",
    "        f\"{COLLOCATION_PATH} not found. This notebook requires the Phase 1 output; \"\n",
    "        f\"set DATA_DIR to wherever it's mounted. Refusing to generate synthetic data instead.\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "observations = pd.read_csv(OBSERVATIONS_PATH)\n",
    "collocation = pd.read_csv(COLLOCATION_PATH)\n",
    "\n",
    "missing_obs_cols = REQUIRED_OBS_COLS - set(observations.columns)\n",
    "missing_colloc_cols = REQUIRED_COLLOC_COLS - set(collocation.columns)\n",
    "if missing_obs_cols:\n",
    "    raise ValueError(f\"observations.csv is missing required column(s): {missing_obs_cols}\")\n",
    "if missing_colloc_cols:\n",
    "    raise ValueError(f\"collocation.csv is missing required column(s): {missing_colloc_cols}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"observations: {len(observations):,} rows, {observations['district'].nunique()} districts, \"\n",
    "      f\"t range [{observations['t'].min():.1f}, {observations['t'].max():.1f}]\")\n",
    "print(f\"collocation: {len(collocation):,} rows, {collocation['district'].nunique()} districts\")\n",
    "print(f\"observations.h: min={observations['h'].min():.2f} max={observations['h'].max():.2f} \"\n",
    "      f\"(depth to water table, m, positive = deeper -- see DATA_DICTIONARY.md)\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0597916f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Recharge fallback for no-humidity districts\n",
    "\n",
    "12 of 38 districts have no humidity data → `R` is NaN in both `observations.csv` and\n",
    "`collocation.csv` for those districts → they contribute **zero rows to the PDE loss**\n",
    "and `S`/`T` cannot receive PDE gradients regardless of `W_PDE`.\n",
    "\n",
    "Fix applied here (not in Phase 1 to avoid regenerating the 368 MB `observations.csv`):\n",
    "load `rainfall_daily.csv` from the same `DATA_DIR`, aggregate to monthly district means,\n",
    "and fill NaN `R` values in `collocation` using the simplified formula\n",
    "\n",
    "    R_fallback = max(rainfall_mm - ET_K * 50, 0)\n",
    "\n",
    "where `ET_K * 50` is the ET proxy at 50 % RH — the middle of the plausible Tamil Nadu\n",
    "range — used in place of the missing humidity reading.  This is a rough approximation,\n",
    "explicitly logged below; it is strictly better than leaving `R = NaN` (= no PDE signal)\n",
    "for these districts.\n",
    "\n",
    "For Mayiladuthurai and Perambalur (no rainfall either), the state-wide monthly mean\n",
    "`R` from the districts that do have a value is used as a last resort."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a91fe45e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# --- R fallback: rainfall-only proxy for districts with no humidity -------------------------\n",
    "# 10 of the 12 no-humidity districts have rainfall coverage; 2 (Mayiladuthurai, Perambalur)\n",
    "# have neither.  Any NaN R remaining after this block uses the state-wide monthly mean.\n",
    "RAINFALL_PATH = os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"rainfall_daily.csv\")\n",
    "ET_K = 0.1           # must match build_recharge.py\n",
    "ET_MID_HUMIDITY = 50 # proxy: assume 50% RH where humidity is unknown\n",
    "\n",
    "EPOCH_TS = pd.Timestamp(\"1970-01-01\")\n",
    "\n",
    "if os.path.exists(RAINFALL_PATH):\n",
    "    rf = pd.read_csv(RAINFALL_PATH, parse_dates=[\"date\"])\n",
    "    # aggregate to district-month mean rainfall\n",
    "    rf[\"month_ts\"] = rf[\"date\"].values.astype(\"datetime64[M]\").astype(\"datetime64[ns]\")\n",
    "    rf[\"month_t\"] = (rf[\"month_ts\"] - EPOCH_TS).dt.total_seconds() / 86400.0\n",
    "    rf_monthly = (rf.groupby([\"canonical_district\", \"month_t\"], as_index=False)[\"rainfall_mm\"].mean()\n",
    "                    .rename(columns={\"canonical_district\": \"district\"}))\n",
    "    # R_fallback = max(rainfall - ET_proxy_at_mid_humidity, 0)\n",
    "    rf_monthly[\"R_fallback\"] = (rf_monthly[\"rainfall_mm\"] - ET_K * (100 - ET_MID_HUMIDITY)).clip(lower=0)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # merge onto collocation -- only fills where collocation's t matches a month_t in rainfall\n",
    "    before_fill = collocation[\"R\"].isna().sum()\n",
    "    collocation = collocation.merge(rf_monthly[[\"district\",\"month_t\",\"R_fallback\"]],\n",
    "                                    left_on=[\"district\",\"t\"], right_on=[\"district\",\"month_t\"],\n",
    "                                    how=\"left\").drop(columns=[\"month_t\"])\n",
    "    collocation[\"R\"] = collocation[\"R\"].fillna(collocation[\"R_fallback\"])\n",
    "    collocation = collocation.drop(columns=[\"R_fallback\"])\n",
    "    after_fill = collocation[\"R\"].isna().sum()\n",
    "    print(f\"R fallback (rainfall-only): filled {before_fill - after_fill:,} of {before_fill:,} NaN R rows \"\n",
    "          f\"in collocation using rainfall_daily.csv\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f\"WARNING: {RAINFALL_PATH} not found -- rainfall R-fallback skipped. \"\n",
    "          f\"12 no-humidity districts will still contribute zero PDE rows.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Last resort: any remaining NaN R gets the state-wide monthly mean R from known districts\n",
    "still_nan = collocation[\"R\"].isna().sum()\n",
    "if still_nan > 0:\n",
    "    state_monthly_mean = (collocation.dropna(subset=[\"R\"])\n",
    "                          .groupby(\"t\")[\"R\"].mean().rename(\"R_state_mean\"))\n",
    "    collocation = collocation.join(state_monthly_mean, on=\"t\")\n",
    "    collocation[\"R\"] = collocation[\"R\"].fillna(collocation[\"R_state_mean\"])\n",
    "    collocation = collocation.drop(columns=[\"R_state_mean\"])\n",
    "    print(f\"State-monthly-mean fallback: filled remaining {still_nan:,} R NaNs \"\n",
    "          f\"(Mayiladuthurai, Perambalur, or any unmatched rows)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "n_nan_after = collocation[\"R\"].isna().sum()\n",
    "print(f\"Collocation R NaNs after all fallbacks: {n_nan_after} \"\n",
    "      f\"({'none -- all districts now have PDE coverage' if n_nan_after == 0 else 'some remain, check above'})\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b55c0f34",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Elevation lookup (depth -> head)\n",
    "\n",
    "`h` in `observations.csv` is depth-to-water below the local ground surface, but the PDE governs\n",
    "*hydraulic head* -- two wells with the same head can have very different depth-to-water if their\n",
    "ground elevations differ (STATUS.md issue 2/4). No DEM ships in `data/raw/`, so this cell fetches\n",
    "ground elevation at runtime for every unique `(lon, lat)` point across both `observations` and the\n",
    "`collocation` grid (~4,000 points total), from the free [Open Topo Data](https://www.opentopodata.org/)\n",
    "SRTM 30m API -- no key required, but **this needs internet access**: on Kaggle, turn on\n",
    "`Settings > Internet` for the notebook, or this cell raises immediately (no synthetic fallback, per\n",
    "CLAUDE.md).\n",
    "\n",
    "Results are cached to `ELEVATION_CACHE_PATH` so a kernel restart doesn't re-fetch from scratch.\n",
    "Points the API can't resolve (e.g. large water bodies) come back `null`; those rows are dropped\n",
    "from both frames (count printed), not zero-filled.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Design note (post-mortem on the first head-conversion run)**: `elev` is fed into the network as\n",
    "an explicit **input** feature (see Model section below), not only used to build the `head` target.\n",
    "The first attempt used it target-side only -- Tamil Nadu's elevation spans ~2,400m (coastal plains\n",
    "to the Nilgiris), so `head = elev - h` inherited nearly all of that range, and the network had no\n",
    "way to predict it since it never saw elevation, only `(x, y, t, district)`. It fit training wells\n",
    "fine but blew up on held-out wells in high-relief districts (RMSE 130m vs. the 12m baseline) --\n",
    "it was forced to blindly reconstruct terrain instead of just fitting the (much smoother) water\n",
    "table. Feeding `elev` in directly lets the network read the terrain off instead of memorizing it.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "114913e5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def xy_key(df):\n",
    "    return df[\"x\"].round(5).astype(str) + \"_\" + df[\"y\"].round(5).astype(str)\n",
    "\n",
    "observations[\"xy_key\"] = xy_key(observations)\n",
    "collocation[\"xy_key\"] = xy_key(collocation)\n",
    "\n",
    "all_xy = (pd.concat([observations[[\"xy_key\", \"x\", \"y\"]], collocation[[\"xy_key\", \"x\", \"y\"]]])\n",
    "          .drop_duplicates(subset=\"xy_key\").reset_index(drop=True))\n",
    "print(f\"{len(all_xy):,} unique (lon, lat) points need elevation (observations + collocation grid)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "if os.path.exists(ELEVATION_CACHE_PATH):\n",
    "    elev_cache = pd.read_csv(ELEVATION_CACHE_PATH)\n",
    "    print(f\"loaded {len(elev_cache):,} cached elevations from {ELEVATION_CACHE_PATH}\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    elev_cache = None   # built fresh below from fetched_rows -- NOT pd.DataFrame(columns=[...]),\n",
    "                         # which has no data to infer dtype from and leaves \"elev\" as `object`;\n",
    "                         # concatenating fetched (float) rows onto that silently poisons the\n",
    "                         # whole column to `object`, which then breaks every downstream numeric\n",
    "                         # op (head, elevhat, headhat) and torch.tensor() with a confusing error.\n",
    "                         # Only shows up on a truly fresh cache -- a reload from CSV self-heals,\n",
    "                         # since read_csv infers proper dtypes -- so this only bites the first run.\n",
    "\n",
    "to_fetch = all_xy if elev_cache is None else all_xy[~all_xy[\"xy_key\"].isin(elev_cache[\"xy_key\"])].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "print(f\"{len(to_fetch):,} points not yet cached, fetching from {ELEVATION_API_URL}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "fetched_rows = []\n",
    "for start in range(0, len(to_fetch), ELEVATION_BATCH_SIZE):\n",
    "    chunk = to_fetch.iloc[start:start + ELEVATION_BATCH_SIZE]\n",
    "    locations = \"|\".join(f\"{lat:.5f},{lon:.5f}\" for lon, lat in zip(chunk[\"x\"], chunk[\"y\"]))\n",
    "\n",
    "    for attempt in range(1, ELEVATION_MAX_RETRIES + 1):\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            resp = requests.get(ELEVATION_API_URL, params={\"locations\": locations}, timeout=30)\n",
    "            resp.raise_for_status()\n",
    "            results = resp.json()[\"results\"]\n",
    "            break\n",
    "        except (requests.RequestException, ValueError) as e:\n",
    "            if attempt == ELEVATION_MAX_RETRIES:\n",
    "                raise RuntimeError(\n",
    "                    f\"elevation API failed after {ELEVATION_MAX_RETRIES} attempts on batch \"\n",
    "                    f\"{start}-{start + len(chunk)}: {e}. If this is Kaggle, check that \"\n",
    "                    f\"Settings > Internet is turned on for this notebook.\"\n",
    "                ) from e\n",
    "            time.sleep(2 ** attempt)\n",
    "\n",
    "    if len(results) != len(chunk):\n",
    "        raise ValueError(f\"elevation API returned {len(results)} results for {len(chunk)} points\")\n",
    "    for key, r in zip(chunk[\"xy_key\"], results):\n",
    "        fetched_rows.append({\"xy_key\": key, \"elev\": r[\"elevation\"]})\n",
    "\n",
    "    time.sleep(ELEVATION_RATE_LIMIT_S)\n",
    "    done = min(start + ELEVATION_BATCH_SIZE, len(to_fetch))\n",
    "    if (start // ELEVATION_BATCH_SIZE) % 5 == 0 or done == len(to_fetch):\n",
    "        print(f\"  fetched {done:,}/{len(to_fetch):,}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "if fetched_rows:\n",
    "    new_elev = pd.DataFrame(fetched_rows)\n",
    "    elev_cache = pd.concat([elev_cache, new_elev], ignore_index=True) if elev_cache is not None else new_elev\n",
    "    elev_cache.to_csv(ELEVATION_CACHE_PATH, index=False)\n",
    "    print(f\"cached {len(fetched_rows):,} new elevations to {ELEVATION_CACHE_PATH}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# belt-and-braces: guarantee numeric dtype regardless of how elev_cache was assembled above\n",
    "elev_cache[\"elev\"] = pd.to_numeric(elev_cache[\"elev\"], errors=\"coerce\")\n",
    "\n",
    "n_null = elev_cache[\"elev\"].isna().sum()\n",
    "if n_null:\n",
    "    print(f\"*** {n_null:,} of {len(elev_cache):,} points returned null elevation \"\n",
    "          f\"(likely off SRTM coverage, e.g. large water bodies) -- DROPPED, not zero-filled ***\")\n",
    "\n",
    "observations = observations.merge(elev_cache, on=\"xy_key\", how=\"left\")\n",
    "collocation = collocation.merge(elev_cache, on=\"xy_key\", how=\"left\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# elev is now used as a MODEL INPUT everywhere below (not just the target conversion), so both\n",
    "# frames need it non-null before any tensors are built -- dropped here, once, not deferred to\n",
    "# individual cells.\n",
    "n_obs_before, n_colloc_before = len(observations), len(collocation)\n",
    "observations = observations.dropna(subset=[\"elev\"]).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "collocation = collocation.dropna(subset=[\"elev\"]).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "print(f\"observations: dropped {n_obs_before - len(observations):,} of {n_obs_before:,} rows with \"\n",
    "      f\"no elevation match; {len(observations):,} remain\")\n",
    "print(f\"collocation: dropped {n_colloc_before - len(collocation):,} of {n_colloc_before:,} rows \"\n",
    "      f\"with no elevation match; {len(collocation):,} remain\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# depth-to-water -> hydraulic head estimate (meters, same vertical datum as elev)\n",
    "observations[\"head\"] = observations[\"elev\"] - observations[\"h\"]\n",
    "print(f\"head: mean={observations['head'].mean():.2f}m std={observations['head'].std():.2f}m \"\n",
    "      f\"(elev mean={observations['elev'].mean():.2f}m, h mean={observations['h'].mean():.2f}m)\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6af2bd14",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Preprocessing\n",
    "\n",
    "- Drop observations outside `[H_MIN, H_MAX]` -- Phase 1's `|h| >= 200` sentinel cut is too\n",
    "  loose (see config cell). Counts are printed; nothing is silently filled or clipped. Applied\n",
    "  to raw depth `h`, ahead of the head conversion above -- this is a bad-reading filter, not a\n",
    "  head/depth judgment call.\n",
    "- Convert lon/lat to local meters (equirectangular approximation around the domain's mean\n",
    "  latitude) -- training directly in degree-space would make the PDE's `S`/`T` parameters\n",
    "  physically meaningless, since 1 degree of longitude and 1 degree of latitude are not the\n",
    "  same distance.\n",
    "- Normalize (x_m, y_m, t_day, elev_m) to roughly [-1, 1] for network stability; the scale\n",
    "  constants are kept so PDE derivatives can be converted back to physical units via the chain\n",
    "  rule. `elev` is normalized the same way as the spatial inputs since it's fed into the network\n",
    "  as an input feature now (see elevation lookup cell), not just used to build the target.\n",
    "- **Normalize the target `head` (`head_c`, `head_s`)**: the network predicts standardized\n",
    "  `headhat`, not raw meters, and not raw depth `h` -- see the elevation cell above for why\n",
    "  head is the physically correct target for the PDE. `pde_residual()` and the evaluation cell\n",
    "  convert back to physical units (and, at the two display boundaries, back to depth-to-water\n",
    "  via `elev`) so nothing downstream is silently in the wrong unit.\n",
    "- Build a district -> integer index map from the union of both files (sorted, so it's\n",
    "  reproducible run to run).\n",
    "- Collocation rows with no `R` (see DATA_DICTIONARY.md -- 12 of 38 districts have no humidity\n",
    "  coverage) are dropped for the PDE loss: the residual is undefined without a real R value, and\n",
    "  filling it with 0 would silently assert \"no recharge\" for districts that were simply never\n",
    "  measured.\n",
    "- Held-out split is by **well** (unique rounded (x, y) location), not by row, to avoid a\n",
    "  station's readings leaking between train and test across time.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d78bd809",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# --- h range filter (see config cell for why the Phase 1 cut isn't enough) ---\n",
    "n_before = len(observations)\n",
    "out_of_range = ~observations[\"h\"].between(H_MIN, H_MAX)\n",
    "print(f\"h range filter [{H_MIN}, {H_MAX}]: dropping {out_of_range.sum():,} of {n_before:,} rows \"\n",
    "      f\"({100 * out_of_range.mean():.2f}%)\")\n",
    "print(f\"  below {H_MIN}: {(observations['h'] < H_MIN).sum():,} rows   \"\n",
    "      f\"above {H_MAX}: {(observations['h'] > H_MAX).sum():,} rows\")\n",
    "observations = observations[~out_of_range].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "print(f\"  kept {len(observations):,} rows; h now spans \"\n",
    "      f\"[{observations['h'].min():.2f}, {observations['h'].max():.2f}], std {observations['h'].std():.3f}m\")\n",
    "\n",
    "REF_LAT = observations[\"y\"].mean()\n",
    "REF_LON = observations[\"x\"].mean()\n",
    "M_PER_DEG_LAT = 110_540.0\n",
    "M_PER_DEG_LON = 111_320.0 * math.cos(math.radians(REF_LAT))\n",
    "\n",
    "def to_local_meters(lon, lat):\n",
    "    x_m = (lon - REF_LON) * M_PER_DEG_LON\n",
    "    y_m = (lat - REF_LAT) * M_PER_DEG_LAT\n",
    "    return x_m, y_m\n",
    "\n",
    "for df in (observations, collocation):\n",
    "    df[\"x_m\"], df[\"y_m\"] = to_local_meters(df[\"x\"], df[\"y\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "# district -> index, built from the union of both files so an index is never missing\n",
    "all_districts = sorted(set(observations[\"district\"]) | set(collocation[\"district\"]))\n",
    "district_to_idx = {d: i for i, d in enumerate(all_districts)}\n",
    "NUM_DISTRICTS = len(all_districts)\n",
    "for df in (observations, collocation):\n",
    "    df[\"district_idx\"] = df[\"district\"].map(district_to_idx)\n",
    "print(f\"{NUM_DISTRICTS} districts indexed\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# normalization constants from the training-relevant range (observations define the domain)\n",
    "x_c, x_s = observations[\"x_m\"].mean(), observations[\"x_m\"].std()\n",
    "y_c, y_s = observations[\"y_m\"].mean(), observations[\"y_m\"].std()\n",
    "t_c, t_s = observations[\"t\"].mean(), observations[\"t\"].std()\n",
    "elev_c, elev_s = observations[\"elev\"].mean(), observations[\"elev\"].std()\n",
    "head_c, head_s = observations[\"head\"].mean(), observations[\"head\"].std()\n",
    "h_c, h_s = observations[\"h\"].mean(), observations[\"h\"].std()\n",
    "# R/Q normalization -- R is NaN for ~80% of rows (pre-2021, no-humidity districts);\n",
    "# fill with 0 (no-recharge baseline) for those rows.\n",
    "R_c = observations[\"R\"].fillna(0.0).mean()\n",
    "R_s = observations[\"R\"].fillna(0.0).std()\n",
    "Q_c = observations[\"Q\"].mean()\n",
    "Q_s = observations[\"Q\"].std()\n",
    "print(f\"x_s={x_s:.1f}m  y_s={y_s:.1f}m  t_s={t_s:.1f}days  elev_c={elev_c:.1f}m  elev_s={elev_s:.1f}m  \"\n",
    "      f\"head_c={head_c:.3f}m  head_s={head_s:.3f}m  h_c={h_c:.3f}m  h_s={h_s:.3f}m\")\n",
    "print(\"  (chain-rule scale constants -- pde_residual and the eval cell both convert back to physical units)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- Run 11: the network now predicts normalized DEPTH h, not normalized HEAD -------------------\n",
    "# Measured on the real data (4.53M rows after the elev merge and the h filter):\n",
    "#   corr(head, elev) = 0.99866, and elev alone accounts for ~100% of head's variance.\n",
    "# head = elev - h, and `elev` is ALREADY A NETWORK INPUT (elevhat), so predicting head let the\n",
    "# network score well by echoing an input. The quantity we actually care about, h, is only\n",
    "# h_s/head_s = 5.2% of the target's std and 0.27% of its VARIANCE -- so MSE on normalized head\n",
    "# barely registers depth errors at all. That is the mechanism behind the saturating band in\n",
    "# every pred_vs_actual.png from Run 7 on: the loss was nearly indifferent to it.\n",
    "# Predicting h directly makes the loss 373x more sensitive to the same physical error.\n",
    "# This costs NOTHING physically -- see pde_residual, where the residual is algebraically the\n",
    "# same quantity as before.\n",
    "print(f\"target: normalized h (depth). head_s/h_s = {head_s / h_s:.1f}x, \"\n",
    "      f\"variance ratio {(head_s / h_s) ** 2:.0f}x -- see comment above\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- Run 22: SEASONAL PHASE features ---------------------------------------------\n",
    "# The delta must be a periodic function of time: TN's water table has a strong, well-known\n",
    "# annual monsoon cycle (recharge roughly May-Dec, drawdown Jan-Apr). A smooth MLP of `t`\n",
    "# alone cannot represent a stiff annual sine, so the model cheated by extrapolating the\n",
    "# monotone trend into the ~1.2yr forecast window (that is exactly what Run 18's pure-AIC\n",
    "# trend became). Give it the phase explicitly, wrapped to [0, 2pi) over the real year:\n",
    "#    seas_sin = sin(2*pi*doy/365.25),  seas_cos = cos(2*pi*doy/365.25)\n",
    "# These are bounded in [-1,1], fully periodic, and identical for collocation points\n",
    "# (which already span every season), so no new normalization is needed.\n",
    "def seasonal_phase(t_days):\n",
    "    # t is already days-since-epoch; day-of-year = t mod 365.25 (no leap-bookkeeping needed)\n",
    "    doy = np.mod(t_days, 365.25)\n",
    "    return np.sin(2 * np.pi * doy / 365.25), np.cos(2 * np.pi * doy / 365.25)\n",
    "\n",
    "obs_sin, obs_cos = seasonal_phase(observations[\"t\"].to_numpy())\n",
    "colloc_sin, colloc_cos = seasonal_phase(collocation[\"t\"].to_numpy())\n",
    "observations[\"seas_sin\"], observations[\"seas_cos\"] = obs_sin, obs_cos\n",
    "collocation[\"seas_sin\"], collocation[\"seas_cos\"] = colloc_sin, colloc_cos\n",
    "print(\"added seas_sin/seas_cos (annual monsoon phase) to observations and collocation\")\n",
    "\n",
    "for df in (observations, collocation):\n",
    "    df[\"xhat\"] = (df[\"x_m\"] - x_c) / x_s\n",
    "    df[\"yhat\"] = (df[\"y_m\"] - y_c) / y_s\n",
    "    df[\"that\"] = (df[\"t\"] - t_c) / t_s\n",
    "    df[\"elevhat\"] = (df[\"elev\"] - elev_c) / elev_s\n",
    "    df[\"Rhat\"] = (df[\"R\"].fillna(R_c) - R_c) / R_s\n",
    "    df[\"Qhat\"] = (df[\"Q\"] - Q_c) / Q_s\n",
    "observations[\"hhat\"] = (observations[\"h\"] - h_c) / h_s   # network predicts this, not raw meters\n",
    "\n",
    "# well = unique rounded (lon, lat) location, since observations.csv has no station-id column\n",
    "observations[\"well_id\"] = (observations[\"x\"].round(5).astype(str) + \"_\" + observations[\"y\"].round(5).astype(str))\n",
    "unique_wells = observations[\"well_id\"].unique()\n",
    "rng = np.random.default_rng(SEED)\n",
    "held_out_wells = set(rng.choice(unique_wells, size=int(len(unique_wells) * HELD_OUT_WELL_FRACTION), replace=False))\n",
    "is_held_out = observations[\"well_id\"].isin(held_out_wells)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Run 12: three-way split. The well holdout above is UNCHANGED from Runs 7-11 (same SEED, same\n",
    "# rng draw order) so the spatial metric stays directly comparable to every prior run.\n",
    "t_cutoff = observations[\"t\"].quantile(TEMPORAL_CUTOFF_QUANTILE)\n",
    "\n",
    "train_df = observations[~is_held_out & (observations[\"t\"] < t_cutoff)].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# FORECAST test set (primary): wells the model trained on, at times it never saw. The\n",
    "# \"well appears in train_df\" filter is what makes this a forecast rather than a cold start --\n",
    "# it drops wells whose records end before the cutoff (mostly pre-2021 manual stations), which\n",
    "# would otherwise be spatial generalization smuggled into the forecast number.\n",
    "trained_wells = set(train_df[\"well_id\"])\n",
    "test_forecast_df = observations[\n",
    "    ~is_held_out & (observations[\"t\"] >= t_cutoff) & observations[\"well_id\"].isin(trained_wells)\n",
    "].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# SPATIAL test set (secondary): held-out wells, all t. Identical to Runs 7-11's `test_df`.\n",
    "test_spatial_df = observations[is_held_out].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"{len(unique_wells)} unique wells -> {len(held_out_wells)} held out for the spatial task\")\n",
    "print(f\"t_cutoff = {t_cutoff:.0f}d (~{1970 + t_cutoff / 365.25:.1f}), \"\n",
    "      f\"quantile {TEMPORAL_CUTOFF_QUANTILE}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  train           {len(train_df):>10,} rows  {train_df['well_id'].nunique():>5} wells  \"\n",
    "      f\"(kept wells, t < cutoff)\")\n",
    "print(f\"  test/forecast   {len(test_forecast_df):>10,} rows  \"\n",
    "      f\"{test_forecast_df['well_id'].nunique():>5} wells  (kept wells, t >= cutoff, seen in train)\")\n",
    "print(f\"  test/spatial    {len(test_spatial_df):>10,} rows  \"\n",
    "      f\"{test_spatial_df['well_id'].nunique():>5} wells  (held-out wells, all t)\")\n",
    "n_dropped = len(observations) - len(train_df) - len(test_forecast_df) - len(test_spatial_df)\n",
    "print(f\"  unused          {n_dropped:>10,} rows  (kept wells past the cutoff whose well never \"\n",
    "      f\"appears before it -- excluded, not folded into either test set)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ic_cutoff = train_df[\"t\"].min() + IC_WINDOW_DAYS\n",
    "ic_df = train_df[train_df[\"t\"] <= ic_cutoff]\n",
    "print(f\"{len(ic_df):,} rows within {IC_WINDOW_DAYS} days of the training set's earliest \"\n",
    "      f\"timestamp, used as the IC term\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- Run 19: per-well baseline anchor feature --------------------------------\n",
    "# 73.6% of h's variance is BETWEEN-well (STATUS.md twelfth-run entry) and is not spatially\n",
    "# smooth.  The forecast task's persistence baseline (5.50m) wins precisely because it knows\n",
    "# each well's LAST OBSERVED DEPTH BEFORE THE CUTOFF -- a single number per well that no\n",
    "# (x,y,elev) feature can express.  Run 18 tried to learn that as a per-well embedding and\n",
    "# overfit it (see config cell).  Run 19 instead feeds the anchor directly: h0 = that last\n",
    "# pre-cutoff depth (normalized to h0hat), one scalar input per row.  For held-out wells\n",
    "# (spatial task) and all collocation points there is no trustworthy anchor, so h0hat = 0\n",
    "# (= the global-mean depth in normalized units) -- the model falls back to district + spatial\n",
    "# features there, exactly as in Runs 12-17, keeping the spatial metric honest.\n",
    "# The anchor uses ONLY train-window data (t < t_cutoff), so the forecast metric cannot leak.\n",
    "well_last_tr = train_df.sort_values(\"t\").groupby(\"well_id\")[\"h\"].last().rename(\"h0\")\n",
    "for df in (train_df, test_forecast_df, test_spatial_df, ic_df):\n",
    "    df[\"h0\"] = df[\"well_id\"].map(well_last_tr)\n",
    "    df[\"h0hat\"] = (df[\"h0\"].fillna(h_c) - h_c) / h_s   # NaN (held-out wells) -> global mean -> 0\n",
    "print(f\"anchor feature: {train_df['well_id'].nunique():,} train wells get their pre-cutoff \"\n",
    "      f\"last depth as input; {test_forecast_df['well_id'].nunique():,} forecast wells reuse it; \"\n",
    "      f\"{len(test_spatial_df):,} held-out rows and all collocation get h0hat=0\")\n",
    "\n",
    "colloc_df = collocation.dropna(subset=[\"R\"]).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "print(f\"{len(colloc_df):,} of {len(collocation):,} collocation rows have a real R value \"\n",
    "      f\"and are used for the PDE loss; the rest (districts with no humidity coverage) are dropped, not zero-filled\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Run 12: R is derived from OBSERVED rainfall, so collocation points at t >= t_cutoff would leak\n",
    "# future forcing into the weights and inflate the forecast metric. Cut them.\n",
    "# This deliberately leaves the forecast window physics-unconstrained -- the network extrapolates\n",
    "# there on its own. The alternative (keep future collocation and treat R as a known scenario\n",
    "# input) is defensible for a \"what-if given this rainfall\" model, but must NOT be used for a\n",
    "# headline forecast number, so it is not the default here.\n",
    "n_colloc_before = len(colloc_df)\n",
    "colloc_df = colloc_df[colloc_df[\"t\"] < t_cutoff].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "print(f\"collocation restricted to t < t_cutoff for the forecast split: dropped \"\n",
    "      f\"{n_colloc_before - len(colloc_df):,} of {n_colloc_before:,} rows; {len(colloc_df):,} remain\")\n",
    "colloc_df[\"h0hat\"] = 0.0   # collocation points are not monitored wells (no anchor)\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- temporal importance weights for training batches ---------------------------\n",
    "# 3.75M of 4.58M observation rows are 6-hourly telemetry from 2021-2026, so a\n",
    "# uniform random batch would see pre-2021 manual readings very rarely.  Weights\n",
    "# are inverse to the number of training rows per calendar year, so each year\n",
    "# contributes roughly equal gradient signal regardless of how densely sampled it is.\n",
    "train_df[\"year\"] = (train_df[\"t\"] / 365.25 + 1970).astype(int)  # approx year from days-since-epoch\n",
    "year_counts = train_df[\"year\"].value_counts()\n",
    "inv_freq = 1.0 / year_counts\n",
    "train_weights_np = train_df[\"year\"].map(inv_freq).to_numpy().astype(\"float32\")\n",
    "train_weights_np /= train_weights_np.sum()   # normalize to sum=1 for multinomial\n",
    "train_weights = torch.tensor(train_weights_np, device=device)\n",
    "print(f\"Temporal importance weights: {year_counts.min()} (min) .. {year_counts.max()} (max) rows/year \"\n",
    "      f\"across {len(year_counts)} years -- sampling will equalize year-level contribution\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "8dc092fb",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def to_tensor(df, cols, dtype=torch.float32):\n",
    "    return torch.tensor(df[cols].to_numpy(), dtype=dtype, device=device)\n",
    "\n",
    "def make_data_tensors(df):\n",
    "    xhat = to_tensor(df, [\"xhat\"])\n",
    "    yhat = to_tensor(df, [\"yhat\"])\n",
    "    that = to_tensor(df, [\"that\"])\n",
    "    elevhat = to_tensor(df, [\"elevhat\"])\n",
    "    rhat = to_tensor(df, [\"Rhat\"])\n",
    "    qhat = to_tensor(df, [\"Qhat\"])\n",
    "    h0hat = to_tensor(df, [\"h0hat\"])   # Run 19: per-well pre-cutoff anchor (0 = no anchor)\n",
    "    seas_sin = to_tensor(df, [\"seas_sin\"])   # Run 22: annual monsoon phase, in [-1,1]\n",
    "    seas_cos = to_tensor(df, [\"seas_cos\"])\n",
    "    district_idx = torch.tensor(df[\"district_idx\"].to_numpy(), dtype=torch.long, device=device)\n",
    "    hhat = to_tensor(df, [\"hhat\"])   # normalized depth target; the eval cell converts back to meters\n",
    "    return xhat, yhat, that, elevhat, rhat, qhat, seas_sin, seas_cos, h0hat, district_idx, hhat\n",
    "\n",
    "def make_colloc_tensors(df):\n",
    "    xhat = to_tensor(df, [\"xhat\"])\n",
    "    yhat = to_tensor(df, [\"yhat\"])\n",
    "    that = to_tensor(df, [\"that\"])\n",
    "    elevhat = to_tensor(df, [\"elevhat\"])\n",
    "    rhat = to_tensor(df, [\"Rhat\"])\n",
    "    qhat = to_tensor(df, [\"Qhat\"])\n",
    "    h0hat = to_tensor(df, [\"h0hat\"])\n",
    "    seas_sin = to_tensor(df, [\"seas_sin\"])   # Run 22\n",
    "    seas_cos = to_tensor(df, [\"seas_cos\"])\n",
    "    district_idx = torch.tensor(df[\"district_idx\"].to_numpy(), dtype=torch.long, device=device)\n",
    "    R = to_tensor(df, [\"R\"])\n",
    "    Q = to_tensor(df, [\"Q\"])\n",
    "    return xhat, yhat, that, elevhat, rhat, qhat, seas_sin, seas_cos, h0hat, district_idx, R, Q\n",
    "\n",
    "train_tensors = make_data_tensors(train_df)\n",
    "test_forecast_tensors = make_data_tensors(test_forecast_df)\n",
    "test_spatial_tensors = make_data_tensors(test_spatial_df)\n",
    "ic_tensors = make_data_tensors(ic_df)\n",
    "colloc_tensors = make_colloc_tensors(colloc_df)\n",
    "print(\"All tensors moved to\", device)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "361b3d4a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Model\n",
    "\n",
    "MLP: `(xhat, yhat, that, elevhat, rhat, qhat, district_embedding) -> hhat`, where `hhat` is\n",
    "normalized depth-to-water (Run 11 switched from head to depth target). `elevhat` is fed in as a\n",
    "plain input feature\n",
    "(normalized like `xhat`/`yhat`/`that`), not just used to build the target -- Tamil Nadu's ~2,400m\n",
    "of relief would otherwise have to be blindly reconstructed by the network from `(x, y, t,\n",
    "district)` alone, which is what broke the first head-conversion run (see elevation lookup cell).\n",
    "`S` and `T` are one learnable scalar per district each (the inverse-problem unknowns), passed\n",
    "through `softplus` to keep them positive -- transmissivity and storage coefficient are physically\n",
    "non-negative.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Update (post Run 8)**: hidden-layer activation is now `SiLU`, not `Tanh`. Run 8 raised `W_PDE`\n",
    "100x (`1e-6 -> 1e-4`) and `T` stayed byte-identical to Run 7's frozen `softplus(0)` init across\n",
    "all 38 districts -- the PDE-loss curve was flat noise for the full 20,000 steps, not slowly\n",
    "converging. `T` only receives gradient through the Laplacian term in `pde_residual()`; `Tanh`'s\n",
    "second derivative is exactly zero at its own zero (`tanh''(0) = 0`), and `WEIGHT_DECAY` keeps\n",
    "this network's pre-activations small (near that zero) almost everywhere, so the Laplacian -- and\n",
    "therefore `T`'s only gradient path -- was structurally starved regardless of loss weight. `SiLU`\n",
    "has the same smoothness and doesn't share that zero-curvature point, so it should let a real\n",
    "Laplacian develop if one is representable at all. See the training-loop cell for the diagnostics\n",
    "(`|laplacian|`, `|T_raw.grad|`) added to confirm this before trusting any `S`/`T` output."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "c82cf492",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class PINN(nn.Module):\n",
    "    def __init__(self, num_districts, emb_dim=EMBEDDING_DIM, hidden_dim=HIDDEN_WIDTH, num_hidden_layers=NUM_HIDDEN_LAYERS):\n",
    "        super().__init__()\n",
    "        self.district_embedding = nn.Embedding(num_districts, emb_dim)\n",
    "        # Run 20: RESIDUAL-FROM-ANCHOR form.  The MLP predicts the normalized DEVIATION\n",
    "        # (h - h0) / h_s from the well's pre-cutoff anchor, and forward() adds the anchor\n",
    "        # back:  hhat = h0hat + mlp(...).  At init (mlp ~ 0) the model IS persistence, so\n",
    "        # the loss gradient goes entirely into learning the trend on top of the anchor --\n",
    "        # the direct attack on the 1.27m forecast gap to persistence.  h0hat stays in the\n",
    "        # input too, so the net can tell whether it is anchored: with H0_DROPOUT_P it also\n",
    "        # sees the unanchored (h0hat=0) case in training, where its output must be the\n",
    "        # absolute field -- which is exactly what held-out wells and collocation need.\n",
    "        # Run 22: input dim 7 -> 9: x,y,t,elev,R,Q + seas_sin,seas_cos + h0hat + district embedding = 17.\n",
    "        layers = []\n",
    "        prev = 9 + emb_dim   # xhat, yhat, that, elevhat, rhat, qhat, seas_sin, seas_cos, h0hat + district embedding\n",
    "        for _ in range(num_hidden_layers):\n",
    "            layers.append(nn.Linear(prev, hidden_dim))\n",
    "            layers.append(nn.SiLU())   # swapped from Tanh after Run 8 (STATUS.md): Tanh's second\n",
    "                                        # derivative is exactly zero at z=0 (tanh''(0) = -2*tanh(0)*(1-tanh(0)^2) = 0),\n",
    "                                        # and WEIGHT_DECAY keeps pre-activations near 0 almost everywhere, so the\n",
    "                                        # Laplacian term in pde_residual() vanished and starved T's only gradient\n",
    "                                        # path regardless of W_PDE. SiLU''(0) = 0.5 != 0 -- same smoothness/domain,\n",
    "                                        # no special init required, but doesn't share Tanh's zero-curvature point.\n",
    "            prev = hidden_dim\n",
    "        layers.append(nn.Linear(prev, 1))\n",
    "        self.mlp = nn.Sequential(*layers)\n",
    "        # inverse-problem parameters: raw (pre-softplus) S, T, one scalar per district\n",
    "        self.S_raw = nn.Parameter(torch.zeros(num_districts))\n",
    "        self.T_raw = nn.Parameter(torch.zeros(num_districts))\n",
    "\n",
    "    def forward(self, xhat, yhat, that, elevhat, rhat, qhat, seas_sin, seas_cos, h0hat, district_idx):\n",
    "        emb = self.district_embedding(district_idx)\n",
    "        inp = torch.cat([xhat, yhat, that, elevhat, rhat, qhat, seas_sin, seas_cos, h0hat, emb], dim=1)\n",
    "        return h0hat + self.mlp(inp)   # residual-from-anchor: mlp learns h - h0\n",
    "\n",
    "    def get_S(self, district_idx):\n",
    "        return F.softplus(self.S_raw[district_idx]).unsqueeze(1)\n",
    "\n",
    "    def get_T(self, district_idx):\n",
    "        return F.softplus(self.T_raw[district_idx]).unsqueeze(1)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "model = PINN(NUM_DISTRICTS).to(device)\n",
    "print(model)\n",
    "print(f\"Trainable parameters: {sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters()):,}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "957ce875",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## PDE residual\n",
    "\n",
    "`S(x,y) * dh/dt = div(T(x,y) * grad(h)) + R - Q`. `S` and `T` are per-district constants (not\n",
    "smooth spatial fields), so their own spatial gradient is zero within a district and\n",
    "`div(T * grad(h))` simplifies to `T * laplacian(h)` -- this drops any boundary-flux term at\n",
    "district edges, a modeling simplification worth being aware of, not a bug.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Update**: this equation governs *hydraulic head*, and the network now predicts head (`elev - h`,\n",
    "see the elevation lookup cell), not raw depth-to-water -- previously `h` here was depth, so two\n",
    "adjacent wells with different ground elevations had different depth-to-water but the same head,\n",
    "and a chunk of the spatial variation the PDE \"saw\" was really surface topography (STATUS.md issue\n",
    "2/4, the leading suspect for why `pde` never converged in any prior run). `elevhat` is passed into\n",
    "the model as a **fixed covariate** here -- `xhat`/`yhat`/`that` get `requires_grad_(True)` so\n",
    "`torch.autograd.grad` can differentiate head w.r.t. them, but `elevhat` does not, so `d(head)/dx`\n",
    "means \"how head changes moving in x while holding this point's elevation fixed,\" the standard way\n",
    "to feed an auxiliary field into a PINN without it absorbing the PDE's own spatial derivatives.\n",
    "One caveat remains: SRTM is a surface model, not bare-earth -- in canopy/urban cells it measures\n",
    "treetop/rooftop height, not true ground elevation, so `elev` is an approximation.\n",
    "\n",
    "Second derivatives are computed via `torch.autograd.grad` with `create_graph=True` (so the\n",
    "graph survives for the backward pass through the loss). Inputs are normalized (`xhat`, `yhat`,\n",
    "`that`) and so is the output (`headhat`), so derivatives are taken w.r.t. those and converted back\n",
    "to physical units via the chain rule: `d/dx_m = (1/x_s) * d/dxhat` and `dhead = head_s * dheadhat`,\n",
    "hence `d^2head/dx_m^2 = (head_s / x_s^2) * d^2headhat/dxhat^2`.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Update (Run 9, the diffusion-term fix)**: `pde_residual` now returns `laplacian` alongside\n",
    "`residual`, purely as a training-time diagnostic (see training-loop/loss-curves cells), and the\n",
    "residual multiplies the diffusion term by `LAPLACIAN_SCALE` (config cell). A local smoke test with\n",
    "the new diagnostic showed why Run 8 (`W_PDE` raised 100x) still left `T` byte-identical to Run 7's\n",
    "frozen init: the chain-rule factor `head_s / x_s^2` (head varies ~200m; `x` spans Tamil Nadu's\n",
    "~700km width in meters, so `x_s ~ 91,000m`) shrinks the physical Laplacian to ~1e-11, about 11\n",
    "orders of magnitude smaller than `R`/`Q` -- `T`'s only gradient path (`-T_d * laplacian`) was\n",
    "structurally invisible to the optimizer, independent of `W_PDE` or activation choice.\n",
    "`LAPLACIAN_SCALE` counteracts this by scaling only the diffusion term's contribution to the\n",
    "residual (not `T_d`'s own parametrization, which stays `softplus(T_raw)` as before) -- see the\n",
    "config cell's full derivation and the important caveat there: `R`/`Q` are documented proxies\n",
    "without true SI calibration, so the resulting `T` should be read as a *relative* quantity\n",
    "(compare districts to each other) rather than literal m²/day transmissivity."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "fbd532d0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def pde_residual(model, xhat, yhat, that, elevhat, rhat, qhat, seas_sin, seas_cos, h0hat, district_idx, R, Q):\n",
    "    xhat = xhat.clone().requires_grad_(True)\n",
    "    yhat = yhat.clone().requires_grad_(True)\n",
    "    that = that.clone().requires_grad_(True)\n",
    "    # elevhat, rhat, qhat, h0hat, seas_sin, seas_cos are NOT made to require grad -- they're\n",
    "    # fixed covariates, not differentiated (see pde_residual rationale cells). Collocation points\n",
    "    # carry h0hat = 0 (no anchor), so this is the pure physics field there.\n",
    "\n",
    "    hhat = model(xhat, yhat, that, elevhat, rhat, qhat, seas_sin, seas_cos, h0hat, district_idx)   # normalized depth\n",
    "    ones = torch.ones_like(hhat)\n",
    "\n",
    "    dhhat_dxhat = torch.autograd.grad(hhat, xhat, grad_outputs=ones, create_graph=True)[0]\n",
    "    dhhat_dyhat = torch.autograd.grad(hhat, yhat, grad_outputs=ones, create_graph=True)[0]\n",
    "    dhhat_dthat = torch.autograd.grad(hhat, that, grad_outputs=ones, create_graph=True)[0]\n",
    "\n",
    "    d2hhat_dxhat2 = torch.autograd.grad(dhhat_dxhat, xhat, grad_outputs=torch.ones_like(dhhat_dxhat), create_graph=True)[0]\n",
    "    d2hhat_dyhat2 = torch.autograd.grad(dhhat_dyhat, yhat, grad_outputs=torch.ones_like(dhhat_dyhat), create_graph=True)[0]\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Chain rule back to physical units, then depth -> head. The network predicts normalized\n",
    "    # hhat, so h = hhat*h_s + h_c and d h/d(.) = h_s * d hhat/d(.) -- the additive h_c drops out\n",
    "    # of every derivative.\n",
    "    dh_dt = h_s * dhhat_dthat / t_s                          # d h(m) / d t(days)\n",
    "    d2h_dx2 = h_s * d2hhat_dxhat2 / (x_s ** 2)                # d2 h(m) / d x(m)^2\n",
    "    d2h_dy2 = h_s * d2hhat_dyhat2 / (y_s ** 2)                # d2 h(m) / d y(m)^2\n",
    "\n",
    "    # head = elev - h. This residual is ALGEBRAICALLY IDENTICAL to Run 10's, not an approximation:\n",
    "    #  - elev is time-invariant, so d head/dt = -d h/dt exactly.\n",
    "    #  - `elevhat` is deliberately excluded from the autograd graph above (it always has been --\n",
    "    #    see the comment at the top of this function), so Run 10's `laplacian` was already the\n",
    "    #    fixed-elev PARTIAL second derivative of head, and at fixed elev d2 head/dx2 = -d2 h/dx2.\n",
    "    #    The terrain-curvature term d2 elev/dx2 was never in the residual and is not being\n",
    "    #    dropped here; switching the target does not lose any physics that was previously present.\n",
    "    # Net effect: both terms flip sign relative to Run 10, and their magnitudes are unchanged.\n",
    "    dhead_dt = -dh_dt\n",
    "    laplacian = -(d2h_dx2 + d2h_dy2)\n",
    "\n",
    "    S_d = model.get_S(district_idx)\n",
    "    T_d = model.get_T(district_idx)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # S*dhead/dt - T*laplacian(head) - R + Q == 0 at a true solution\n",
    "    # LAPLACIAN_SCALE (config cell, added for Run 9) multiplies only the diffusion term's\n",
    "    # CONTRIBUTION TO THE RESIDUAL, not laplacian itself or T_d's parametrization -- see the\n",
    "    # config cell's long comment for why: the physical `laplacian` is ~1e-11 (chain-rule\n",
    "    # shrinkage over Tamil Nadu's ~700km extent), ~11 orders of magnitude smaller than R/Q,\n",
    "    # so T's gradient was invisible to the optimizer regardless of W_PDE or activation choice.\n",
    "    residual = S_d * dhead_dt - LAPLACIAN_SCALE * T_d * laplacian - R + Q\n",
    "    # laplacian is returned UNSCALED, purely as a training-time diagnostic (see training loop\n",
    "    # cell) -- this keeps the printed/plotted |laplacian| interpretable as the actual physical\n",
    "    # second derivative, separate from whatever multiplier the residual applies to make T\n",
    "    # learnable.\n",
    "    return residual, laplacian\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "732299c1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Loss\n",
    "\n",
    "`L = W_DATA * MSE(h_pred, h_true) + W_PDE * MSE(pde_residual) + W_IC * MSE(ic_mismatch)`, components logged separately.\n",
    "Two extra diagnostics are logged alongside (not part of the loss): `laplacian_abs_mean` and\n",
    "`t_grad_norm` (`T_raw.grad.norm()`), added after Run 8 left `T` frozen with no visible signal in\n",
    "the existing loss curves as to why -- see the PDE residual and training-loop cells."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f25d7edc",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def sample_batch(tensors, batch_size, generator=None, weights=None):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Sample a mini-batch from a tuple of tensors (all same first dimension).\n",
    "\n",
    "    If `weights` is provided (a 1-D float tensor of the same length), samples\n",
    "    are drawn proportionally to those weights -- used for temporal importance\n",
    "    sampling so that years with fewer readings contribute equally to each batch.\n",
    "    Without weights, falls back to uniform random sampling.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    n = tensors[0].shape[0]\n",
    "    k = min(batch_size, n)\n",
    "    if weights is not None:\n",
    "        idx = torch.multinomial(weights, k, replacement=True, generator=generator)\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        idx = torch.randint(0, n, (k,), device=device, generator=generator)\n",
    "    return tuple(t[idx] for t in tensors)\n",
    "\n",
    "def anchor_dropout(h0hat):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Run 20: zero the anchor on a random H0_DROPOUT_P fraction of TRAINING rows, in\n",
    "    BOTH the input slot and the additive residual (same tensor).  forward() returns\n",
    "    h0hat + mlp(...), so zeroing makes the MLP predict the absolute field for that row --\n",
    "    which is exactly the held-out-well and collocation case.  This keeps h0hat=0 in\n",
    "    distribution so the spatial metric no longer regresses (Run 19: 13.45m).\"\"\"\n",
    "    if H0_DROPOUT_P > 0 and model.training:\n",
    "        keep = (torch.rand(h0hat.shape[0], 1, device=h0hat.device) >= H0_DROPOUT_P).float()\n",
    "        return h0hat * keep\n",
    "    return h0hat\n",
    "\n",
    "def compute_losses(model, data_batch, colloc_batch, ic_batch):\n",
    "    xhat, yhat, that, elevhat, rhat, qhat, seas_sin, seas_cos, h0hat, d_idx, h_true = data_batch\n",
    "    h0hat_used = anchor_dropout(h0hat)\n",
    "    h_pred = model(xhat, yhat, that, elevhat, rhat, qhat, seas_sin, seas_cos, h0hat_used, d_idx)\n",
    "    data_loss = F.mse_loss(h_pred, h_true)\n",
    "    # Run 21: delta regularization.  forward() returns h0hat + mlp(...), so the MLP's\n",
    "    # deviation-from-anchor IS h_pred - h0hat_used.  Penalizing its mean square shrinks\n",
    "    # the learned trend toward zero unless the data justifies it (see W_DELTA config).\n",
    "    delta = h_pred - h0hat_used\n",
    "    delta_loss = torch.mean(delta ** 2)\n",
    "\n",
    "    xhat_i, yhat_i, that_i, elevhat_i, rhat_i, qhat_i, seas_sin_i, seas_cos_i, h0hat_i, d_idx_i, h_true_i = ic_batch\n",
    "    h_pred_i = model(xhat_i, yhat_i, that_i, elevhat_i, rhat_i, qhat_i, seas_sin_i, seas_cos_i, anchor_dropout(h0hat_i), d_idx_i)\n",
    "    ic_loss = F.mse_loss(h_pred_i, h_true_i)\n",
    "\n",
    "    xhat_c, yhat_c, that_c, elevhat_c, rhat_c, qhat_c, seas_sin_c, seas_cos_c, h0hat_c, d_idx_c, R_c, Q_c = colloc_batch\n",
    "    residual, laplacian = pde_residual(model, xhat_c, yhat_c, that_c, elevhat_c, rhat_c, qhat_c, seas_sin_c, seas_cos_c, h0hat_c, d_idx_c, R_c, Q_c)\n",
    "    pde_loss = torch.mean(residual ** 2)\n",
    "    # diagnostic only -- not part of the loss (see pde_residual and training-loop cells)\n",
    "    laplacian_abs_mean = laplacian.detach().abs().mean().item()\n",
    "\n",
    "    total = W_DATA * data_loss + W_PDE * pde_loss + W_IC * ic_loss + W_DELTA * delta_loss\n",
    "    components = {\"data\": data_loss.item(), \"pde\": pde_loss.item(), \"ic\": ic_loss.item(), \"delta\": delta_loss.item(), \"total\": total.item(),\n",
    "                  \"laplacian_abs_mean\": laplacian_abs_mean}\n",
    "    return total, components\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f1fbe9c8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Training loop\n",
    "\n",
    "Adam + step LR schedule, loss components printed every `PRINT_EVERY` epochs."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "ca07d537",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Run 11 fix (STATUS.md tenth-run entry): S_raw/T_raw are PHYSICAL inverse-problem parameters,\n",
    "# not network weights, and were previously caught by the blanket weight_decay on\n",
    "# model.parameters(). Weight decay pulls *_raw toward 0, i.e. pulls S/T toward the arbitrary\n",
    "# constant softplus(0)=0.6931 -- regularizing a physical quantity toward an arbitrary value is\n",
    "# wrong regardless of scale. T escaped it in Run 10 only because LAPLACIAN_SCALE made its\n",
    "# gradient big enough to overcome the pull; S, whose gradient is near zero, was held at init by\n",
    "# it. Split into param groups so decay still regularizes the MLP (where it is doing real work\n",
    "# against well memorization -- see WEIGHT_DECAY) but not S_raw/T_raw.\n",
    "physical_params = [model.S_raw, model.T_raw]\n",
    "physical_ids = {id(p) for p in physical_params}\n",
    "network_params = [p for p in model.parameters() if id(p) not in physical_ids]\n",
    "optimizer = torch.optim.Adam(\n",
    "    [{\"params\": network_params, \"weight_decay\": WEIGHT_DECAY},\n",
    "     {\"params\": physical_params, \"weight_decay\": 0.0}],\n",
    "    lr=ADAM_LR,\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(f\"optimizer: {sum(p.numel() for p in network_params):,} network params \"\n",
    "      f\"(weight_decay={WEIGHT_DECAY}) + {sum(p.numel() for p in physical_params):,} physical \"\n",
    "      f\"S/T params (weight_decay=0)\")\n",
    "scheduler = torch.optim.lr_scheduler.StepLR(optimizer, step_size=LR_STEP_SIZE, gamma=LR_GAMMA)\n",
    "\n",
    "history = {\"data\": [], \"pde\": [], \"ic\": [], \"delta\": [], \"total\": [], \"laplacian_abs_mean\": [],\n",
    "           \"t_grad_norm\": [], \"s_grad_norm\": []}\n",
    "\n",
    "model.train()\n",
    "for epoch in range(N_EPOCHS_ADAM):\n",
    "    data_batch = sample_batch(train_tensors, BATCH_SIZE_DATA, weights=train_weights)\n",
    "    colloc_batch = sample_batch(colloc_tensors, BATCH_SIZE_COLLOC)\n",
    "    ic_batch = sample_batch(ic_tensors, BATCH_SIZE_IC)\n",
    "\n",
    "    optimizer.zero_grad()\n",
    "    total_loss, components = compute_losses(model, data_batch, colloc_batch, ic_batch)\n",
    "    total_loss.backward()\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Diagnostic for the Run 8 finding (STATUS.md): T only gets gradient through the Laplacian\n",
    "    # term in the PDE residual, and Run 8 (W_PDE raised 100x, 1e-6 -> 1e-4) left T byte-identical\n",
    "    # to Run 7's frozen init anyway -- consistent with a near-zero Laplacian starving T's gradient\n",
    "    # regardless of loss weight. Logged every step (cheap, one .norm() call) so loss_curves.png\n",
    "    # shows directly whether the Tanh -> SiLU swap above fixed it, instead of inferring it after\n",
    "    # the fact from a suspiciously round S/T value the way Run 8 was diagnosed.\n",
    "    t_grad_norm = model.T_raw.grad.norm().item() if model.T_raw.grad is not None else float(\"nan\")\n",
    "    components[\"t_grad_norm\"] = t_grad_norm\n",
    "    # Run 11: the S-side twin of the above. Run 10 left S within 4.3e-04 of softplus(0) while T\n",
    "    # moved 3.135 (7,300x further), and the leading hypothesis is that S's only gradient path --\n",
    "    # the UNSCALED `S_d * dhead_dt` term in pde_residual -- is starved against R/Q at O(1-20),\n",
    "    # the same way T's was before LAPLACIAN_SCALE. That was never measured, only inferred. This\n",
    "    # settles it: if |S_raw.grad| is ~1e-14 float noise, S needs its own scale multiplier\n",
    "    # (Next step 2); if it is healthy and S still doesn't move, the diagnosis is wrong and the\n",
    "    # weight-decay fix above was the whole story.\n",
    "    s_grad_norm = model.S_raw.grad.norm().item() if model.S_raw.grad is not None else float(\"nan\")\n",
    "    components[\"s_grad_norm\"] = s_grad_norm\n",
    "\n",
    "    optimizer.step()\n",
    "    scheduler.step()\n",
    "\n",
    "    for k, v in components.items():\n",
    "        history[k].append(v)\n",
    "\n",
    "    if epoch % PRINT_EVERY == 0 or epoch == N_EPOCHS_ADAM - 1:\n",
    "        lr_now = scheduler.get_last_lr()[0]\n",
    "        # data/ic are MSE in NORMALIZED DEPTH units (Run 11); the meters-of-depth equivalent is\n",
    "        # printed alongside. This IS now directly comparable to the held-out RMSE in the eval cell\n",
    "        # (same quantity, no elev round-trip) -- the gap between them is the generalization gap.\n",
    "        data_rmse_h_m = (components[\"data\"] ** 0.5) * h_s\n",
    "        print(f\"epoch {epoch:6d}  lr={lr_now:.2e}  data={components['data']:.4f} ({data_rmse_h_m:5.2f}m depth)  \"\n",
    "              f\"pde={components['pde']:.4f}  ic={components['ic']:.4f}  delta={components['delta']:.4f}  total={components['total']:.4f}  \"\n",
    "              f\"|laplacian|={components['laplacian_abs_mean']:.2e}  |T_raw.grad|={t_grad_norm:.2e}  \"\n",
    "              f\"|S_raw.grad|={s_grad_norm:.2e}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d3cfb1c7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Optional L-BFGS fine-tune\n",
    "\n",
    "A short second-order pass on a large fixed batch, common for PINNs once Adam has roughly converged."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "31dd52e9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if RUN_LBFGS_FINETUNE:\n",
    "    lbfgs_data = sample_batch(train_tensors, min(20000, train_tensors[0].shape[0]))\n",
    "    lbfgs_colloc = sample_batch(colloc_tensors, min(20000, colloc_tensors[0].shape[0]))\n",
    "    lbfgs_ic = sample_batch(ic_tensors, min(4000, ic_tensors[0].shape[0]))\n",
    "\n",
    "    lbfgs_opt = torch.optim.LBFGS(model.parameters(), max_iter=LBFGS_MAX_ITER,\n",
    "                                  line_search_fn=\"strong_wolfe\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    def closure():\n",
    "        lbfgs_opt.zero_grad()\n",
    "        loss, components = compute_losses(model, lbfgs_data, lbfgs_colloc, lbfgs_ic)\n",
    "        loss.backward()\n",
    "        # same diagnostic as the Adam loop -- must come after backward() for T_raw.grad to exist\n",
    "        components[\"t_grad_norm\"] = model.T_raw.grad.norm().item() if model.T_raw.grad is not None else float(\"nan\")\n",
    "        components[\"s_grad_norm\"] = model.S_raw.grad.norm().item() if model.S_raw.grad is not None else float(\"nan\")\n",
    "        closure.last_components = components\n",
    "        return loss\n",
    "\n",
    "    lbfgs_opt.step(closure)\n",
    "    c = closure.last_components\n",
    "    print(f\"L-BFGS finished: data={c['data']:.4f}  pde={c['pde']:.4f}  ic={c['ic']:.4f}  total={c['total']:.4f}  \"\n",
    "          f\"|laplacian|={c['laplacian_abs_mean']:.2e}  |T_raw.grad|={c['t_grad_norm']:.2e}  \"\n",
    "          f\"|S_raw.grad|={c['s_grad_norm']:.2e}\")\n",
    "    for k in history:\n",
    "        history[k].append(c[k])\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"Skipped L-BFGS fine-tune (RUN_LBFGS_FINETUNE=False)\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "bf5e8cc7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 4, figsize=(24, 8))\n",
    "loss_keys = [\"data\", \"pde\", \"ic\", \"delta\", \"total\"]\n",
    "diag_keys = [\"laplacian_abs_mean\", \"t_grad_norm\", \"s_grad_norm\"]   # Run 8/11 diagnostics, see pde_residual/training-loop cells\n",
    "for ax, key in zip(axes.ravel(), loss_keys + diag_keys):\n",
    "    ax.plot(history[key])\n",
    "    if key in loss_keys:\n",
    "        ax.set_yscale(\"log\")\n",
    "        ax.set_title(f\"{key} loss\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        ax.set_title(key)   # linear scale -- these can legitimately hit 0, which log-scale can't show\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel(\"step\")\n",
    "for ax in axes.ravel()[len(loss_keys) + len(diag_keys):]:\n",
    "    ax.axis(\"off\")   # 2x4 grid, 7 series -- hide the spare slot\n",
    "fig.tight_layout()\n",
    "fig.savefig(os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, \"loss_curves.png\"), dpi=120)\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "948fc776",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Evaluation on held-out wells\n",
    "\n",
    "Held out **by well** (see preprocessing cell), not by row, so no station leaks between train\n",
    "and test across time. The network predicts normalized head; predictions are converted back to\n",
    "head in meters (`* head_s + head_c`), then to **depth-to-water** via `elev` (`h_pred = elev -\n",
    "head_pred`) so this run's RMSE/MAE stay in the same units as every prior run and the baselines\n",
    "below -- `h_true` is taken directly from `test_df[\"h\"]`, not reconstructed from `elev`, so\n",
    "ground-truth values carry no elevation-lookup error.\n",
    "\n",
    "Scored against trivial baselines fitted on the training wells only. This matters: the first\n",
    "three runs (RMSE 15.6-18.3m) all *lost* to predicting a single constant (13.3m) or the district\n",
    "mean (12.95m), which is not visible from the loss curves alone. A PINN that can't beat the\n",
    "district mean isn't learning a useful field, whatever its loss says."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d273a479",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "model.eval()\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def rmse(pred, true):\n",
    "    return float(np.sqrt(np.mean((np.asarray(pred) - np.asarray(true)) ** 2)))\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def mae(pred, true):\n",
    "    return float(np.mean(np.abs(np.asarray(pred) - np.asarray(true))))\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def predict_h(tensors):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Network output -> depth-to-water in meters. Direct since Run 11: the network predicts h\n",
    "    itself, so nothing cancels through a ~200m elevation term on the way to the metric.\"\"\"\n",
    "    with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "        xhat, yhat, that, elevhat, rhat, qhat, seas_sin, seas_cos, h0hat, d_idx, _ = tensors\n",
    "        hhat_pred = model(xhat, yhat, that, elevhat, rhat, qhat, seas_sin, seas_cos, h0hat, d_idx)\n",
    "    return hhat_pred.cpu().numpy().ravel() * h_s + h_c\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def report(name, test_df_, tensors, baselines, note=\"\"):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Score the PINN against a dict of {label: prediction array} on one test set.\"\"\"\n",
    "    h_pred = predict_h(tensors)\n",
    "    h_true = test_df_[\"h\"].to_numpy()\n",
    "    m_rmse, m_mae = rmse(h_pred, h_true), mae(h_pred, h_true)\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n=== {name} ===\")\n",
    "    print(f\"{len(test_df_):,} rows over {test_df_['well_id'].nunique():,} wells\" + (f\"  {note}\" if note else \"\"))\n",
    "    print()\n",
    "    w = max(len(l) for l in baselines) + 10\n",
    "    print(f\"  {'predictor':<{w}} {'RMSE (m)':>10} {'MAE (m)':>10}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  {'-' * (w + 22)}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  {'PINN':<{w}} {m_rmse:>10.3f} {m_mae:>10.3f}\")\n",
    "    for label, pred in baselines.items():\n",
    "        print(f\"  {('baseline: ' + label):<{w}} {rmse(pred, h_true):>10.3f} {mae(pred, h_true):>10.3f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    best_label = min(baselines, key=lambda k: rmse(baselines[k], h_true))\n",
    "    best = rmse(baselines[best_label], h_true)\n",
    "    print()\n",
    "    if m_rmse < best:\n",
    "        print(f\"  PINN beats the best baseline ({best_label}) by {best - m_rmse:.3f}m RMSE.\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print(f\"  *** PINN LOSES to the best baseline ({best_label}) by {m_rmse - best:.3f}m RMSE. ***\")\n",
    "    return h_pred, h_true, m_rmse, m_mae, best_label, best\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "global_mean = train_df[\"h\"].mean()\n",
    "district_mean = train_df.groupby(\"district\")[\"h\"].mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "# PRIMARY: forecast task -- wells the model trained on, at times it never saw.\n",
    "# Baselines are all fitted on train_df only. Persistence and the final-year mean are the ones\n",
    "# that matter: a groundwater forecast that cannot beat \"assume it stays where it was\" is not\n",
    "# forecasting anything. Local diagnostics put these at ~5.61m / ~5.55m and the oracle floor\n",
    "# (each well's own mean within the test period) at 3.73m.\n",
    "# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "fc = test_forecast_df\n",
    "well_mean_tr = train_df.groupby(\"well_id\")[\"h\"].mean()\n",
    "persistence = train_df.sort_values(\"t\").groupby(\"well_id\")[\"h\"].last()\n",
    "final_year = train_df[train_df[\"t\"] >= t_cutoff - 365].groupby(\"well_id\")[\"h\"].mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "fc_baselines = {\n",
    "    \"persistence (last obs before cutoff)\": fc[\"well_id\"].map(persistence).fillna(global_mean).to_numpy(),\n",
    "    \"final-year mean before cutoff\": fc[\"well_id\"].map(final_year).fillna(global_mean).to_numpy(),\n",
    "    \"per-well mean (train period)\": fc[\"well_id\"].map(well_mean_tr).fillna(global_mean).to_numpy(),\n",
    "    \"district mean\": fc[\"district\"].map(district_mean).fillna(global_mean).to_numpy(),\n",
    "    \"global mean\": np.full(len(fc), global_mean),\n",
    "}\n",
    "fc_pred, fc_true, fc_rmse, fc_mae, fc_best_label, fc_best = report(\n",
    "    \"FORECAST (primary): known wells, t >= cutoff\", fc, test_forecast_tensors, fc_baselines,\n",
    "    note=f\"| oracle floor {rmse(fc['well_id'].map(fc.groupby('well_id')['h'].mean()), fc['h']):.2f}m\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "# SECONDARY: spatial task -- held-out wells, all t. Same split as Runs 7-11, so the number is\n",
    "# directly comparable. The kNN baseline is the one that matters here: it scores ~11.62m, versus\n",
    "# the PINN's best-ever 11.51m, which is what showed this task is at its feature ceiling. The\n",
    "# district mean (12.07m) is too weak a bar and hid that for eleven runs.\n",
    "# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "sp = test_spatial_df\n",
    "tr_wells = train_df.groupby(\"well_id\").agg(x=(\"x\", \"first\"), y=(\"y\", \"first\"), hbar=(\"h\", \"mean\"))\n",
    "sp_wells = sp.groupby(\"well_id\").agg(x=(\"x\", \"first\"), y=(\"y\", \"first\"))\n",
    "A = np.c_[tr_wells[\"x\"] * M_PER_DEG_LON, tr_wells[\"y\"] * M_PER_DEG_LAT]\n",
    "B = np.c_[sp_wells[\"x\"] * M_PER_DEG_LON, sp_wells[\"y\"] * M_PER_DEG_LAT]\n",
    "D = np.sqrt(((B[:, None, :] - A[None, :, :]) ** 2).sum(-1))     # meters, brute force (~470 x ~2650)\n",
    "KNN_K = 5\n",
    "knn_idx = np.argsort(D, axis=1)[:, :KNN_K]\n",
    "knn_d = np.take_along_axis(D, knn_idx, 1)\n",
    "knn_w = 1.0 / np.maximum(knn_d, 100.0)                          # inverse distance, floored at 100m\n",
    "knn_hat = (tr_wells[\"hbar\"].to_numpy()[knn_idx] * knn_w).sum(1) / knn_w.sum(1)\n",
    "knn_series = pd.Series(knn_hat, index=sp_wells.index)\n",
    "\n",
    "sp_baselines = {\n",
    "    f\"kNN(x,y) on train well means, k={KNN_K}\": sp[\"well_id\"].map(knn_series).fillna(global_mean).to_numpy(),\n",
    "    \"district mean\": sp[\"district\"].map(district_mean).fillna(global_mean).to_numpy(),\n",
    "    \"global mean\": np.full(len(sp), global_mean),\n",
    "}\n",
    "sp_pred, sp_true, sp_rmse, sp_mae, sp_best_label, sp_best = report(\n",
    "    \"SPATIAL (secondary): held-out wells, all t\", sp, test_spatial_tensors, sp_baselines,\n",
    "    note=\"| oracle floor 5.07m | at its feature ceiling, see STATUS.md\")\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(11, 5.5))\n",
    "for ax, (title, ht, hp, r, m, bl, bv) in zip(axes, [\n",
    "        (\"FORECAST (primary)\", fc_true, fc_pred, fc_rmse, fc_mae, fc_best_label, fc_best),\n",
    "        (\"SPATIAL (secondary)\", sp_true, sp_pred, sp_rmse, sp_mae, sp_best_label, sp_best)]):\n",
    "    ax.scatter(ht, hp, s=2, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "    lims = [min(ht.min(), hp.min()), max(ht.max(), hp.max())]\n",
    "    ax.plot(lims, lims, \"r--\", linewidth=1)\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel(\"True h (m, depth to water)\")\n",
    "    ax.set_ylabel(\"Predicted h (m)\")\n",
    "    ax.set_title(f\"{title}: RMSE={r:.2f}m, MAE={m:.2f}m\\nbest baseline ({bl}): {bv:.2f}m\", fontsize=9)\n",
    "fig.tight_layout()\n",
    "fig.savefig(os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, \"pred_vs_actual.png\"), dpi=120)\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ccddb8ba",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Spatial maps at fixed time slices\n",
    "\n",
    "Uses the collocation grid's spatial layout at 3 chosen timestamps, across all 38 districts.\n",
    "R and Q are now network inputs (Run 13), so each grid point carries one representative R/Q\n",
    "from the collocation set. Grid points with no elevation match were already dropped upstream\n",
    "(elevation lookup cell)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a463ddf1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "t_slices = np.quantile(observations[\"t\"].to_numpy(), [0.1, 0.5, 0.9])\n",
    "# R/Q are now network inputs, not just residual terms -- take one representative per grid point.\n",
    "grid_xy = collocation.groupby([\"x\", \"y\", \"x_m\", \"y_m\", \"district_idx\", \"elev\", \"elevhat\"], as_index=False)[[\"R\", \"Q\"]].first()\n",
    "print(f\"spatial map grid: {len(grid_xy):,} points\")\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(16, 5), sharex=True, sharey=True)\n",
    "for ax, t_val in zip(axes, t_slices):\n",
    "    that_val = (t_val - t_c) / t_s\n",
    "    xhat_g = torch.tensor(((grid_xy[\"x_m\"] - x_c) / x_s).to_numpy(), dtype=torch.float32, device=device).unsqueeze(1)\n",
    "    yhat_g = torch.tensor(((grid_xy[\"y_m\"] - y_c) / y_s).to_numpy(), dtype=torch.float32, device=device).unsqueeze(1)\n",
    "    that_g = torch.full_like(xhat_g, that_val)\n",
    "    seas_sin_g, seas_cos_g = seasonal_phase(np.full(len(grid_xy), t_val))   # Run 22\n",
    "    seas_sin_g = torch.tensor(seas_sin_g, dtype=torch.float32, device=device).unsqueeze(1)\n",
    "    seas_cos_g = torch.tensor(seas_cos_g, dtype=torch.float32, device=device).unsqueeze(1)\n",
    "    elevhat_g = torch.tensor(grid_xy[\"elevhat\"].to_numpy(), dtype=torch.float32, device=device).unsqueeze(1)\n",
    "    rhat_g = torch.tensor(((grid_xy[\"R\"].fillna(R_c) - R_c) / R_s).to_numpy(), dtype=torch.float32, device=device).unsqueeze(1)\n",
    "    qhat_g = torch.tensor(((grid_xy[\"Q\"] - Q_c) / Q_s).to_numpy(), dtype=torch.float32, device=device).unsqueeze(1)\n",
    "    d_idx_g = torch.tensor(grid_xy[\"district_idx\"].to_numpy(), dtype=torch.long, device=device)\n",
    "    h0hat_g = torch.zeros(len(grid_xy), dtype=torch.float32, device=device).unsqueeze(1)   # grid = no anchor\n",
    "\n",
    "    with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "        hhat_g = model(xhat_g, yhat_g, that_g, elevhat_g, rhat_g, qhat_g, seas_sin_g, seas_cos_g, h0hat_g, d_idx_g).cpu().numpy().ravel()\n",
    "    h_g = hhat_g * h_s + h_c                                  # -> depth to water, meters (direct)\n",
    "\n",
    "    sc = ax.scatter(grid_xy[\"x\"], grid_xy[\"y\"], c=h_g, cmap=\"viridis_r\", s=25)\n",
    "    ax.set_title(f\"t={t_val:.0f}d\")\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel(\"Longitude\")\n",
    "fig.colorbar(sc, ax=axes, label=\"Predicted h (m, depth to water)\", shrink=0.8)\n",
    "axes[0].set_ylabel(\"Latitude\")\n",
    "fig.savefig(os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, \"spatial_maps.png\"), dpi=120, bbox_inches=\"tight\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "562cf4e3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Save outputs\n",
    "\n",
    "Model weights, learned S/T per district, and the district index map (for reproducibility).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Run 9 caveat**: `T` (not `S`) is now scaled inside the PDE residual by `LAPLACIAN_SCALE`\n",
    "(config cell) so it can receive gradient at all -- see the PDE residual cell. `R`/`Q` are\n",
    "proxy quantities without true SI calibration, so there was never a path to literal m²/day\n",
    "transmissivity from this data; read the `T` column below as a **relative** measure (spread\n",
    "across districts) rather than an absolute physical value."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d3966e0a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "torch.save(model.state_dict(), os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, \"pinn_model.pth\"))\n",
    "\n",
    "with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "    all_idx = torch.arange(NUM_DISTRICTS, device=device)\n",
    "    S_values = F.softplus(model.S_raw).cpu().numpy()\n",
    "    T_values = F.softplus(model.T_raw).cpu().numpy()\n",
    "\n",
    "st_df = pd.DataFrame({\"district\": all_districts, \"S\": S_values, \"T\": T_values})\n",
    "st_df.to_csv(os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, \"learned_S_T_per_district.csv\"), index=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "pd.DataFrame({\"district\": all_districts, \"district_idx\": range(NUM_DISTRICTS)}) \\\n",
    "    .to_csv(os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, \"district_index_map.csv\"), index=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Saved model weights, learned S/T ({len(st_df)} districts), and the district index map to {OUTPUT_DIR}/\")\n",
    "print(st_df.sort_values('T', ascending=False).head())\n"
   ]
  }
